hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1374","Ahmad bin Al-Miqdam Al-Ajli told us, Yazid told us, meaning Ibn Zuray’, Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: We were at The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then the sun eclipsed, so he got up to the mosque dragging his robe from the wheel, and the people lamented at him, so he prayed two rak’ahs as You pray. When it was revealed, he addressed us and said: “Indeed, the sun and the moon are two of the signs of God. For the death of one of the people, so if you see anything of them, pray and pray until what is wrong with you is revealed.”"
